      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Upload any ordinary photo in \"1. Source photo\". The saved example uses the existing local red dress.png image. You do not need to prepare a skeleton or edge map.\n\n2. Choose the conversion in \"2. Choose conversion\". CannyEdgePreprocessor is selected and needs no detector weights. Queue the workflow.\n\n3. The converted guide appears in the preview below the converter; the generated result appears at Save Image on the right. Both preview and ControlNet receive the SAME converted image.\n\nChange the preprocessor dropdown to test a different type without changing any cables. The Qwen Union checkpoint stays the same. Character Creator supplies the target character and scene prompt.\n\nOutput sizing is automatic: the converted guide is scaled to ~1 megapixel, rounded to a 16-pixel grid, and its actual dimensions drive the output latent. Portrait and landscape photos keep their proportions.\n\nThe creator negative_prompt output is connected to negative text encoding. SD/SDXL generate concise style/crop-aware negatives; Qwen currently outputs an empty negative. Disconnect this link to enter your own negative text."
      ],
      "title": "START HERE - ready to queue",
      "color": "#334355",
      "bgcolor": "#202b38"
    },
