    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -650,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        590,
        400
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Use an ordinary photo, render or drawing as the source image. Pick a clear full-body photo for whole-body pose tests; a cropped portrait cannot provide leg joints that are outside the image.\n\nThe AIO Aux Preprocessor actually converts the source image. Its IMAGE output goes to both the guide preview and entry.image; the original photo is not used directly as a guide.\n\nThe workflow reuses the installed comfyui_controlnet_aux package. Canny and Scribble XDoG need no detector weights. Pose, Depth, HED, Realistic Lineart and M-LSD require their own detector weights, which are not installed yet. Those modes need the additional download approved; until then use Canny or Scribble XDoG.\n\nAlready have a prepared guide? Select it in Load Image and choose preprocessor = none. This bypasses conversion."
      ],
      "title": "Photo -> conversion -> guide -> ControlNet",
      "color": "#334355",
      "bgcolor": "#202b38"
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -650,
        440
      ],
      "size": [
        590,
        480
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 7,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "CannyEdgePreprocessor: sharp edges and silhouettes. Ready now; no detector weights.\n\nScribble_XDoG_Preprocessor: converts a photo into rough sketch lines. Ready now; no detector weights.\n\nDWPreprocessor: DWPose body/hand/face skeleton, for pose control. Needs yolox_l.onnx and the DWPose TorchScript detector.\n\nDepthAnythingV2Preprocessor: relative near/far structure. Needs Depth Anything V2 Large (the AIO default).\n\nHEDPreprocessor: broad, soft object edges. Needs ControlNetHED.pth.\n\nLineArtPreprocessor: drawn contours. Needs sk_model.pth and sk_model2.pth.\n\nM-LSDPreprocessor: straight lines for architecture. Needs mlsd_large_512_fp32.pth.\n\nThe AIO dropdown also contains unrelated preprocessors. Use the choices above with this Qwen Union. Its generic SD/SDXL labels do not require switching to SD/SDXL ControlNet weights."
      ],
      "title": "Conversion dropdown - recommended Qwen Union choices",
      "color": "#334355",
      "bgcolor": "#202b38"
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        380,
        200
      ],
      "size": [
        310,
        610
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "strength: 1.0 starts with strong control. Try 0.5-0.8 for more prompt freedom; 0 disables control.\n\nstart_percent / end_percent: the part of denoising that uses the guide. 0 to 1 means the whole run.\n\nConverter resolution (768) controls extraction detail. Guide canvas megapixels (1.0) controls output size. Its dimensions feed Empty Latent Image automatically: do not disconnect those size wires.\n\nThis prevents a portrait skeleton or edge map being stretched to a square output. Adjust megapixels to change detail/cost while keeping the guide aspect ratio.\n\nPrompt framing still needs to agree with the source. A full-body skeleton can compete with a waist-up prompt even when the dimensions match.\n\nMULTIPLE TYPES: use the same source and preprocessing resolution, then match each final guide to this canvas. Share the model patch and VAE; connect the additional entry to the next creator socket."
      ],
      "title": "Strength, cropping and multiple guides",
      "color": "#334355",
      "bgcolor": "#202b38"
    },
